            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "entry_CamwgA": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Maintenance",
            "text": "<p>1. Always check that the shredder and especially the guards are not worn down or damaged but firmly attached before use.</p><p>2. Check that the nuts, bolts and screws are tight.</p><p><strong>Removing Blockages</strong></p><p>1. Use the provided Allen key to release the 4 Allen screws on the housing cover.</p><p>2. Remove the housing cover. This may require light shaking movements. </p><p>3. Always switch the product off, disconnect it from the power supply and let the product cool down before opening the cutter housing.<br/><br/>Always wear protective, heavy gloves and use protective safety equipment when performing blade maintenance. </p><p>4. Remove any blockages.<br/>5. Re-install the housing cover. Make sure the housing cover is fitted correctly so that the<br/>blade shaft, the pressure plate rod and the 4 recesses for the Allen screws are all correctly aligned and fit smoothly into the recesses on the housing cover. </p><p>Ensure that the cutting pressure plate is positioned correctly.</p><p>6. Secure the housing cover firmly with the 4 Allen screws.</p><p>NOTE: The housing cover is safety interlocked, the  shredder will not operate if it is not replaced correctly.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
