    "df696699-42a8-4b2a-8976-674c3e309cd21": {
      "type": "featured-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "entry_b8YQkh": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "How do I adjust the blade gap?",
            "text": "<p>The pressure plate is used in the silent shredder to finely adjust the cutting blade gap and to improve cutting performance as the cutting blade and pressure plate wears.</p><p>During adjustment, the pressure plate can be moved towards or away from the rotating cutting blade. </p><p>To improve cutting performance, the pressure plate is moved towards the rotating cutting blade.</p><p>Also, the pressure plate can be moved away from the cutting blade to help clear blockages.</p><p>The cutting blade may continue to rotate for a few seconds after switching off the shredder.</p><p>1.  Ensure the shredder inlet is free from material to be  shredded.</p><p><br/>2. Start the shredder by turning the switch clockwise. This is the direction required to shred material.</p><p><br/>3. The shredder blade should rotate freely; it has a low speed of rotation only once per second.</p><p>4. Slowly rotate the cutting blade adjustment knob clockwise a 1/2 turn. The pressure plate is advanced towards the blade while the blade is moving.</p><p>5. If the cutting blade continues to rotate without a grinding noise, advance another 1/2 turn.</p><p>6. There will be an audible grinding noise when the pressure plate is being cut by the blade. </p><p>Your shredder is now correctly set up for a good cut. There should be small aluminium shavings from the pressure plate in the collection box.</p><p>Check cutting performance by feeding a woody branch into the shredder. It should be cut through correctly into pieces approximately 3cm in length.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
