        "entry_xbjkUQ": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": false,
            "title": "Why does the shredder keep switching off?",
            "text": "<p>In the event of the shredder being overloaded, e.g. due to branches that are too thick, the shredder may switch off automatically. </p><p>Overload protection will be activated in the following circumstances:</p><p>- a build-up of shredded material around the cutting blade.<br/>- the material being shredded is greater than the motor capacity.<br/>- when there is too much resistance against the cutting blade.</p><p>To reset the shredder: Turn the operation mode selection switch to the middle ‘OFF’ position and press the reset switch. Remove the blockages if necessary. Switch on the shredder again.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
